    "text": "To determine the combined length of the CDs that James buys, we need to calculate the length of each CD and then sum them up.\n\nFirst, we know that two of the CDs are each 1.5 hours long. So, the total length of these two CDs is:\n\\[ 1.5 \\text{ hours} + 1.5 \\text{ hours} = 3 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the length of the third CD. The problem states that the last CD is twice as long as one of the other CDs. Since one of the other CDs is 1.5 hours long, the length of the third CD is:\n\\[ 2 \\times 1.5 \\text{ hours} = 3 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNow, we add the lengths of all three CDs together to find the combined length:\n\\[ 3 \\text{ hours} + 3 \\text{ hours} + 3 \\text{ hours} = 9 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nTherefore, the combined length of the CDs is:\n\\[ \\boxed{9} \\]",
